# FixFlags — Product Intelligence for AI-built products

When asked to scan, test, finish, or review a web app, use the FixFlags MCP tools.

## Setup

User needs Pro/Agency API key and MCP configured (`.cursor/mcp.json`) pointing at `https://fixflags.com/api/mcp` with `x-api-key`.

Copy this rule into the project as `.cursor/rules/fixflags.mdc`, or keep it under `ide-integrations/cursor/`.

## Live MCP tools (canonical)

| Tool | Use |
|------|-----|
| `ff_check_url` | Start a check. Pass `waitForCompletion: true` when you need results inline. |
| `ff_get_check_status` | Poll status / progress |
| `ff_get_report` | Rubric summaries + shareStatus |
| `ff_get_rubric` | Flags + fix text for one rubric (`MESSAGE` \| `EXPERIENCE` \| `REACH`) |
| `ff_get_flag` | Full fix prompt for one flag (`tool`: cursor/claude/lovable/bolt/…) |
| `ff_get_product_context` | Product Contract / Product Intelligence for the report |
| `ff_get_current_finish_plan` | Top Finish Plan items + plan-mode prompt |
| `ff_plan_mode_prompt` | Single plan-mode prompt for the Finish Plan |
| `ff_monitoring` | Re-check same URL (verify fixes) |
| `ff_compare` | Diff two reports |
| `ff_list_recent_audits` | Recent audits |
| `generate-fix-prompt` | Custom fix prompt from a problem description |

There is **no** `ff_get_report_flags` tool. Use `ff_get_rubric` per rubric or `ff_get_flag`.

## Core workflow

1. User gives a public URL (not localhost).
2. Call `ff_check_url` (optionally `waitForCompletion: true`).
3. Call `ff_get_product_context` then `ff_get_current_finish_plan`.
4. Call `ff_get_report` for scores; call `ff_get_rubric` for each rubric for Flags.
5. Present findings by **Message**, **Experience**, **Reach**.
6. Offer to apply the Finish Plan / fix prompt; then suggest `ff_monitoring` re-check.

## Presenting results

For each Flag:
- **Severity**: CRITICAL / IMPORTANT / POLISH
- **Problem** + evidence
- **Fix**: from `ff_get_flag` or rubric flag `fix` field

## Re-checks

After applying fixes, call `ff_monitoring` (or `ff_check_url` on the same URL). Re-checks are free and unlimited on owned reports. Verified clears update Product Intelligence.

## Modes

- Default / critical path: up to ~6 related pages when supported by `ff_check_url` mode
- Single page: `mode: "single"` when the user asks for one URL only
